<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!-- Phone button icons on the 24x24 grid. A function the desktop app also has draws the
         desktop's own glyph (Noctis.UI Assets/Icons.axaml, named in each comment):
         - filled desktop glyphs (Fluent/Material, drawn on the desktop in a 24x24 Canvas or a
           PathIcon) are copied verbatim;
         - the desktop's stroked line icons (MenuLine*, drawn by LineIcon/MenuV2 with a 2.25u
           round stroke) are that stroke expanded to a fill outline, same centre line and width.
         Phone-only functions (download, dismiss chevron, the library list button) keep their own
         glyph: 1.8u stroke (round caps/joins) expanded to fill, 2.0u for the single strokes.
         Every string carries "M0 0ZM24 24Z": two zero-area contours at the grid corners (at the
         end of copied desktop data, so its relative commands keep their meaning). PathIcon draws
         Data with Stretch=Uniform, so without them each glyph would be stretched to its own
         bounds (stroke weight changing from glyph to glyph). With them, a PathIcon's
         Width/Height is the 24-grid box: at 24 a glyph is drawn 1:1, as the desktop's 24 grid.
         Typical boxes: 24 icon buttons and sheet rows, 20 inside pills, 30 mini player
         transport, 36 queue pill transport, 44/54 Now Playing. -->
